{"ts": "2026-11-10T05:15:13+00:00", "move": "critique", "round": 1, "summary": {"attacks": ["A3", "A4"], "dropped": [], "absence_unverified": [], "needed_evidence": ["TfL London-wide ULEZ One Year Report Tables 12 and 42–45: obtain a constant-camera outer-London compliance series, with dates before 29 August 2023 separated from implementation days, and a comparable no-expansion fleet trajectory accounting for natural turnover and earlier-zone spillovers.", "London-wide ULEZ scrappage scheme administrative evaluation: completed vehicle disposals and replacements before 29 August 2023, applicants' vehicle-use locations, and evidence that replacement occurred earlier than it otherwise would have—not merely the scheme launch date or approvals.", "TfL/GLA 2022–2024 outer-London emissions inventory and fleet records: extract bus deployment by route, taxi and PHV vehicle-kilometres and emissions classes, and fixed-coverage heavy-vehicle compliance; compare NOx emissions with the previous ULEZ boundary retained and separate policies continuing.", "Independence note: the differently labelled S1 and S6 origins do not establish independent corroboration. Their taxi, bus and scrappage statements draw on the same GLA/TfL policy administration. E2 and E23 also interpret the same report's fleet observations rather than independently replicate them. Trace the underlying administrative datasets before counting these as separate evidential lines.", "LAQN, LondonAir and AURN ratified annual data for 2022 and 2024: identify roadside stations in the newly covered area, match stations with valid means in both years, and obtain concentrations, data capture, relocations and aggregation weights.", "London-wide ULEZ One Year Report Appendix 3 expansion-specific bootstrap results and Appendix 4 Table 70: retrieve or extract uncertainty for the No London-wide ULEZ comparison, alongside sensitivity to counterfactual start date, fixed-site composition and the 5–40 km control area. Do not substitute Table 67's all-phases uncertainty. The September 2024 and January–September results require period-matched claims rather than C1–C4's full-calendar-year claims.", "For the calendar-2024 claims, find an expansion-specific evaluation covering January–December 2024 that retains earlier ULEZ phases in the counterfactual and reports how meteorology, seasonality, regional background, other policies, anticipation and control-area spillovers are handled."]}, "state_hash": "1928952cc79e531f0e60f75c1373441faa3466945dfc0adf1d7b89dbf98255c1", "prev_hash": "ea73df3ab6b9e14e3b60533ee271ffc3aa7d88d5761eb9cf5c5bbf206234a0ff", "usage": [{"provider": "openai", "model": "gpt-6-astra", "input_tokens": 36820, "output_tokens": 3386, "role": "critic"}], "hash": "7d9fa811a8731fb8b8d0a962b866849aa64610b26bce6998adde709de4a4c230"}
