{"ts": "2026-11-10T05:20:44+00:00", "move": "critique", "round": 2, "summary": {"attacks": [], "dropped": [], "absence_unverified": [], "needed_evidence": ["GLA/TfL expansion-specific roadside NO2 evaluation covering January–December 2024: newly covered outer-London site identifiers, observed and no-expansion annual means, aggregation weights, concentration and percentage effects, and uncertainty intervals. The counterfactual must retain earlier ULEZ phases; S1's September endpoint and all-phases annual estimates do not supply this comparison.", "London Air Quality Network and AURN ratified 2022 and 2024 annual NO2 datasets: identify roadside stations within the newly expanded boundary with valid observations in both years, including data capture, relocations and instrument changes, to calculate the matched-site change required by C5–C7.", "GLA/TfL underlying expansion-specific bootstrap results for the London-wide ULEZ One Year Report, Figure 12 and Table 70: numerical uncertainty for the reported 1.1 µg/m³ or 4.8% September 2024 reduction, distinct from Table 67's all-phases uncertainty, and an explicit distinction between endpoint and first-year-average effects.", "Further improvement in London's air quality demands more …, npj Clean Air: retrieve Supplementary Tables S1, S2, S5 and S6 and Figure 3 numerical data for outer-London traffic-site NO2. Extract the ULEZ3 effect, uncertainty interval, contributing sites and exact averaging period; obtain expansion-specific treatment of anticipation rather than the ULEZ1 anticipation test.", "London-wide ULEZ One Year Report concentration-analysis replication or validation results: pre-announcement outer-London versus 5–40 km control trends, alternative control-zone estimates, sensitivity to counterfactual start dates and fixed-site selection, and adjustment for London-specific taxi, PHV and bus policies. These comparisons are needed to assess whether the estimated divergence isolates expansion effects rather than differential trends.", "Independence note: E148 is derived directly from E22, not an additional observation. For the shared taxi-policy facts, E15 and E126 draw on the same implementing authority's records across two GLA reports and should not be counted as independent corroboration."]}, "state_hash": "dde52ef3d47784e3a52b039a72c711df384f492fa8a7ae95e61be88abc7fecc2", "prev_hash": "62482c47f0e0386153dceb469fe85923905f8df620fe44c90f4d9d496fc58b39", "usage": [{"provider": "openai", "model": "gpt-6-astra", "input_tokens": 38175, "output_tokens": 2014, "role": "critic"}], "hash": "a258e294798aceab8a9b5c3fe73404a04b1dcdcea2e049e58bb38d94ae597de8"}
